        "Name": "Late Unbalanced Bilinguals Dataset: Structural and Functional MRI data with functional localizers",
        "ReferencesAndLinks": null
      },
      "readme": "# Late Unbalanced Bilinguals Dataset\n\nThis dataset contains structural and functional MRI data along with two functional localizer tasks for 119 late, unbalanced, Polish-English bilinguals.\n\nThe dataset includes anatomical T1 scans for each participant.\n\nOn top of anatomical images, for each participant the dataset includes functional scans and their corresponding fieldmaps for two functional localizer tasks:\n\nLanguage localizer in L1 - based on the Alice in Wonderland task (Malik-Moraleda, Ayyash et al., 2022)\nMultiple Demand network localizer - based on a visual working memory task (Fedorenko et al., 2013)\n\nDetails of the functional localizer tasks are described in:\nhttps://direct.mit.edu/nol/article/5/2/315/118227\nhttps://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-023-49375-9\n\nIn case of questions please contact Agata Wolna (agata.wolna@uj.edu.pl / awolna@mit.edu) or Zofia Wodniecka (zofia.wodniecka@uj.edu.pl).\n",
